    "rationale": "Inherent risk is critical because an untrusted inbound email can drive a read of any customer's confidential record followed by an unrestricted external send (TC1 lethal trifecta), with both the CRM and mail credentials broadly scoped and no declared step or runtime limit. Residual drops only to high because the sole control on the path is a single behavioral prompt instruction; no structural control narrows or severs the path, and no human approval gate exists. Forecast returns to critical under model_upgrade, autonomy_increase, longer_task_horizon, or control_removal, any of which defeats the one dependent control that currently provides the only credit. Two property-level gaps compound this: no step or runtime limit on the agent's loop, and weak, unpinned, token-only authentication on both MCP servers."
